+## September 29 solo-first security-console prototype
+
+**Confirmed direction:** Greg approved a solo-first, co-op-enhanced in-world VR security-console prototype. Every required interaction must work for one player without a second operator, voice communication or simultaneous distant actions. Players can turn away and leave. Different controls can be used concurrently; ownership applies to an individually held control, not the whole station.
+
+**Correction and scope:** do not assume Level 1 introduction or a terminal in every level. This supersedes the earlier co-op-dependent/recurring-terminal brainstorming. Production placement remains **Open**. The optional prototype does not expand the Chapter 1 MVP contract or replace Level 2's confirmed personal fuse/power objective. Shared device changes are not shared completion, reset or travel.
+
+**Planned work:** [parent #67](https://github.com/GregStephen/RunawayChimps/issues/67) tracks #68-#73: networked skeleton, physical controls, two shared camera feeds, solo encounter, multiplayer recovery and Quest/playtest acceptance. See [the focused plan](security-console-prototype-plan.md). One monitor/two fixed cameras, latching required access, a primitive threat proxy and a personal endpoint are **proposed prototype defaults**, not final progression or content.
+
+**Pending validation:** no prototype gameplay implementation, Unity test, Photon session, Android build or headset/performance result is supplied by this planning record. Preserve the existing launch terminal, personal Hub controls, recorded surveillance, level objectives, economy and ten-player target. Greg chooses keep/rework/defer after testing; keep does not automatically place the mechanic in a production level.
 
