+## September 29 security-console prototype work plan
+
+**Confirmed planning request:** Greg requested individually actionable issues for a solo-first, co-op-enhanced physical VR security console. Every required action must work for one player without voice communication or a second operator. This optional prototype is separate from the Chapter 1 release queue in #25.
+
+**Planned sequence:** [parent #67](https://github.com/GregStephen/RunawayChimps/issues/67) owns #68 networked walking skeleton, #69 physical controls/per-control ownership, #70 two shared camera feeds, #71 solo encounter/personal completion, #72 multiplayer recovery and #73 solo/two-headset/Quest acceptance. All six are assigned to GregStephen. [The focused plan](security-console-prototype-plan.md) records scope; issues own live acceptance status. Keep one implementation item active and add targeted tests with each slice.
+
+**Integration boundaries:** use a saved development-only graybox scene with the adopted 2022.3.62f3/PUN/Built-in baseline and existing rig/session infrastructure. Inspect/reuse PhysicalButton and loaded-sector authority patterns; #64 owns inherited fingertip/script defects. Do not weaken validators, repurpose the launch terminal, require PR #16's recorded surveillance, change personal progression, or add the console to a production level. One monitor/two cameras, latched required access and a primitive threat proxy are test defaults, not final design commitments.
+
+**Evidence and decision:** planning only; no gameplay, Unity/runtime, Photon, Android or headset/performance test is completed here. #73 requires actual solo usefulness, optional two-headset use and Quest 2/3 measurements before a successful keep decision. Missing devices/tests remain pending; two actors do not certify ten-player operation. Greg chooses keep/rework/defer without expanding MVP scope. Update both maintained documents as actual implementation and evidence arrive.
 
